admin-db-help = Read-only database diagnostics. No credentials or message content are displayed.
admin-db-free-help = Reusable SQLite pages stay inside the file after deletions until space is reclaimed.
admin-db-inspect-help = Detailed inspection can take up to 30 seconds. Table sizes include indexes; PostgreSQL row counts are estimates.
admin-db-limited = Some measurements reached the scan limit or are unavailable on this database.
admin-db-orphan-help = These cached bodies have no message row pointing to them. Inspection does not remove them.

admin-db-growth = Database growth
admin-db-growth-alert = Sustained rapid growth detected. Inspect the largest tables and write origins.
admin-db-growth-warming = Collecting a baseline; at least two samples are needed.
admin-db-growth-normal = No sustained rapid growth detected.
admin-db-growth-rate = Recent growth
admin-db-growth-threshold = Alert threshold
admin-db-origin = Write origin
admin-db-writes = Statements
admin-db-input = Input bytes
admin-db-growth-history = Size history
admin-db-write-help = Write activity over the last 15 minutes, for this server process. Input bytes are bound parameter sizes, not disk growth. Affected rows may include rolled-back transactions. Raw SQL, credentials and message content are excluded. History resets on restart.

admin-db-cleanup = Cleanup
admin-db-log-files = Application log files
admin-db-rotate = Rotate now
admin-db-log-help = Apply configured age, file-count and size limits. Rotation uses the configured compression setting; compression may continue in the background.
admin-db-offline-cleanup = Offline database repair
admin-db-offline-help = Run these commands on the deployment host. Preview changes nothing. Apply stops the app, creates a backup and resumes it afterwards. Compaction needs temporary free disk space. Add --skip-backup only to deliberately omit that copy; purging the index requires a rebuild afterwards.
admin-db-preview-command = Preview cleanup
admin-db-apply-command = Apply cleanup
admin-db-copy-command = Copy command
admin-db-command-copied = Command copied.
admin-db-maintenance-requested = Log maintenance requested.

admin-db-history-range = History period
admin-db-history-all = All available
admin-db-history-help = History starts with this server process. The database chart fits its vertical scale; WAL has a separate scale.
admin-db-payload = Text / binary payload
admin-db-columns = Largest columns
admin-db-live-bytes = Referenced cached body bytes
admin-db-analysis-help = Automatic read-only analysis ranks measured storage consumers. Payload excludes indexes and page overhead; unavailable physical sizes do not hide payload measurements.
admin-db-breakdown = What uses the space
admin-db-history-period = { $from } — { $to }

admin-db-background-title = Background database maintenance
admin-db-background-configure = Configure maintenance
admin-db-background-run = Run a batch
admin-db-background-help = Small batches collect unreferenced bodies after a grace period and reclaim eligible SQLite pages. Live mail stays referenced and is preserved. Status resets on restart.
admin-db-background-result = Scanned: { $scanned } · Removed: { $removed } ({ $bytes }) · Reclaimed pages: { $pages }
admin-db-background-conversion = This existing database needs a one-time offline conversion before incremental reclamation can run. Preview the command without --apply first.
admin-db-background-deferred = Maintenance yielded to a busy database, its work budget, or WAL pressure. It will retry automatically.
admin-db-background-next = Next batch: { $time }
